 "seawant": [],
 "_seawant": "⛔ THE MIRROR OF `landwant`, AND THE ONE THING THE GENERATOR COULD NOT SAY. Every other authored lever ADDS land — `pts`, `landwant`, `bridges`, `short` all raise the field, `belts` add relief, and `umb` is a special-purpose ripple for the Umbral depths. So an ISLAND was always authorable (a `landwant` point) and a BAY was not. ⚑ Each entry is [lat, lon] and SUBTRACTS the same gaussian `landwant` adds, so a point just inside a coast opens an inlet and a point in open land opens a lake basin. ⚠️ A RIVER IS NOT THIS: rivers are `waterauth.authored`, which carves the DEM after the terrain exists. ⛑ EMPTY ON PURPOSE — the world is byte-identical until someone authors into it, and the moment they do, rebuild (`node scripts/world/generate_world.mjs`).",
